RFBridge / HB-RF-ETH
The RFBridge protocol is adapted from Alexander Reinert's HB-RF-ETH firmware,
copyright 2022, under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).
Original source:
https://github.com/alexreinert/HB-RF-ETH/tree/eda7bfe28f95ecabb919e2b1f6100deaaa246cee
Relevant original files: src/rawuartudplistener.cpp,
src/radiomoduleconnector.cpp and src/hmframe.cpp.
Changes: Linux UDP bridge, protocol tests, standard Raspberry Pi PL011 tty
and GPIO-v2 backend, GPIO reset/LED support and HomeLink administration.
The RFBridge adaptation in rfbridge/ retains CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
This is an independent adaptation, not an official HB-RF-ETH/OpenCCU release.

Pi pin assignments checked against the piVCCU device-tree specification:
https://github.com/alexreinert/piVCCU/blob/master/dts/pivccu-raspberrypi.dts
No piVCCU kernel module or OpenCCU operating-system image is included.

ser2net
Corey Minyard and contributors. GPL-2.0 with additional permissions stated
in the original source files. Installed separately from the operating-system
repository or built from the verified upstream 4.6.8 source by the installer.
https://github.com/cminyard/ser2net/tree/v4.6.8
Upstream archive SHA256:
066790a7ed75534808a139d69840a89647e355b887be383b4b1704e2305601a8
The locally built ser2net package includes its complete upstream source archive
and HomeLink build script under /usr/share/doc/ser2net/.

Python, OpenSSL, NetworkManager, OpenSSH, glibc and Raspberry Pi OS are separate
system components; their package copyright and license files remain in place.

HomeLink uses system fonts and no third-party frontend framework.
